+(ns highereds.facts
+  "Cited authority catalogue for the higher-education actor's PERMANENT
+  scope exclusions.
+
+  Why this namespace exists. `highereds.governor/scope-exclusion-violations`
+  used to carry a bare list of twelve English regex fragments (\"grading\",
+  \"disciplin\", \"CPS\", ...) with no record of WHY any of them is excluded
+  or WHO holds the decision instead. That shape has two concrete failure
+  modes an audit cannot recover from:
+
+    1. A held proposal produced the string `\"Scope exclusion: grading\"`.
+       An operator reading the append-only ledger a year later cannot tell
+       whether that hold was legally required or an arbitrary keyword.
+    2. Nothing stopped a future edit from silently deleting a pattern.
+       Deleting `\"expulsion\"` widens the actor's authority over students
+       and every test stays green, because no test asserted the SET.
+
+  So the exclusions are declared here as data: each excluded decision class
+  names the body that actually holds the decision and cites the instrument
+  that puts it there. The governor derives its patterns from this catalogue
+  rather than owning a second copy, and a hold now carries its citations
+  into the ledger.
+
+  Jurisdiction. The cited corpus is Japan (e-Gov 法令検索), because that is
+  the jurisdiction this actor is operated in. An institution elsewhere adds
+  a class or extra `:class/citations` entries for its own instruments; the
+  governor reads whatever is here. `:class/patterns` are deliberately
+  bilingual so the free-text net catches both operating languages.
+
+  Verification. Every citation is machine-checkable against the e-Gov API:
+  `clojure -M:verify-citations` (see `highereds.verify-citations`) fetches
+  each law and asserts the cited article really exists in it. That check is
+  a separate, network-using entry point on purpose -- the unit tests here
+  stay offline and deterministic. **HTTP status alone is not verification**:
+  laws.e-gov.go.jp is a single-page app and answers 200 for a nonexistent
+  law id, so a link-checker that only reads status codes passes on a
+  fabricated citation. The verifier reads the returned law text instead.
+
+  Every article quoted in `:citation/note` below was read from the e-Gov
+  API on 2026-08-08, not recalled."
+  (:require [clojure.string :as str]))
+
+;; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
+;; citation helpers
+;; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+(def egov-law-base "https://laws.e-gov.go.jp/law/")
+(def egov-api-base "https://laws.e-gov.go.jp/api/1/lawdata/")
+
+(defn law-url
+  "Human-readable e-Gov page for a law id."
+  [law-id]
+  (str egov-law-base law-id))
+
+(defn law-api-url
+  "e-Gov API endpoint that returns the full text of a law id. This is what
+  `highereds.verify-citations` reads; the human page is a SPA and cannot be
+  used to prove a citation exists."
+  [law-id]
+  (str egov-api-base law-id))
+
+(defn- cite
+  [law-id instrument instrument-en article note]
+  {:citation/jurisdiction :JP
+   :citation/law-id law-id
+   :citation/instrument instrument
+   :citation/instrument-en instrument-en
+   :citation/article article
+   :citation/note note
+   :citation/url (law-url law-id)
+   :citation/api-url (law-api-url law-id)})
+
+;; law ids used below (e-Gov 法令検索)
+(def ^:private gakko-kyoiku-ho   "322AC0000000026") ; 学校教育法
+(def ^:private gakko-shiko-kisoku "322M40000080011") ; 学校教育法施行規則
+(def ^:private daigaku-setchi    "331M50000080028") ; 大学設置基準
+(def ^:private gakui-kisoku      "328M50000080009") ; 学位規則
+(def ^:private appi              "415AC0000000057") ; 個人情報の保護に関する法律
+
+;; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
+;; the catalogue
+;; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+(def excluded-decision-classes
+  "Decision classes this actor may never take, each with the body that holds
+  the decision instead and the instruments that put it there.
+
+  `:class/patterns` are case-insensitive regex fragments matched against
+  `(str op \" \" description)` by the governor. They are a free-text safety
+  net over an advisor that writes prose -- NOT the primary control. The
+  primary control is the closed operation allowlist in
+  `highereds.operation/valid-operation?`; this net exists because a proposal
+  for an allowed op can still describe an excluded decision."
+  [{:class/id :academic-grading
+    :class/label "Academic grading, assessment and credit award"
+    :class/decided-by
+    "The university, by examination or another method it defines, against
+     assessment criteria published to students in advance."
+    :class/patterns ["grading" "assessment" "credit.?award" "成績評価" "単位認定"]
+    :class/citations
+    [(cite daigaku-setchi "大学設置基準" "Standards for Establishment of Universities"
+           "第二十五条の二"
+           "第2項: 学修の成果に係る評価及び卒業の認定に当たつては、客観性及び厳格性を確保するため、学生に対してその基準をあらかじめ明示するとともに、当該基準にしたがつて適切に行うものとする。")
+     (cite daigaku-setchi "大学設置基準" "Standards for Establishment of Universities"
+           "第二十七条"
+           "大学は、一の授業科目を履修した学生に対しては、試験その他の大学が定める適切な方法により学修の成果を評価して単位を与えるものとする。")]}
+
+   {:class/id :academic-standing
+    :class/label "Academic standing, progression and completion determinations"
+    :class/decided-by
+    "The president (学長), who must hear the faculty council (教授会) on
+     graduation and course completion."
+    :class/patterns ["academic.?standing" "probation" "卒業.?認定" "課程.?修了"]
+    :class/citations
+    [(cite gakko-kyoiku-ho "学校教育法" "School Education Act"
+           "第九十三条"
+           "第2項第1号: 教授会は、学長が「学生の入学、卒業及び課程の修了」について決定を行うに当たり意見を述べるものとする。")
+     (cite gakko-shiko-kisoku "学校教育法施行規則" "Ordinance for Enforcement of the School Education Act"
+           "第百六十五条の二"
+           "第1項第1号: 大学は「卒業又は修了の認定に関する方針」を定めるものとする。")]}
+
+   {:class/id :admissions-decision
+    :class/label "Admissions decisions and selection of entrants"
+    :class/decided-by
+    "The president (学長), who must hear the faculty council (教授会), under
+     the institution's published admissions policy."
+    :class/patterns ["admissions?.*decision" "入学者?選抜" "合否"]
+    :class/citations
+    [(cite gakko-kyoiku-ho "学校教育法" "School Education Act"
+           "第九十三条"
+           "第2項第1号: 教授会は、学長が「学生の入学」について決定を行うに当たり意見を述べるものとする。")
+     (cite gakko-shiko-kisoku "学校教育法施行規則" "Ordinance for Enforcement of the School Education Act"
+           "第百六十五条の二"
+           "第1項第3号: 大学は「入学者の受入れに関する方針」を定めるものとする。")]}
+
+   {:class/id :degree-conferral
+    :class/label "Degree conferral"
+    :class/decided-by
+    "The university (for a bachelor's degree) or the university operating the
+     graduate school (for master's and doctoral degrees)."
+    :class/patterns ["degree.*conferral" "学位.?授与"]
+    :class/citations
+    [(cite gakko-kyoiku-ho "学校教育法" "School Education Act"
+           "第百四条"
+           "第1項: 大学は、文部科学大臣の定めるところにより、大学を卒業した者に対し、学士の学位を授与するものとする。")
+     (cite gakui-kisoku "学位規則" "Degree Regulations"
+           "第二条"
+           "法第104条第1項の規定による学士の学位の授与は、大学が、当該大学を卒業した者に対し行うものとする。")
+     (cite gakui-kisoku "学位規則" "Degree Regulations"
+           "第四条"
+           "法第104条第3項の規定による博士の学位の授与は、大学院を置く大学が、当該大学院の博士課程を修了した者に対し行うものとする。")]}
+
+   {:class/id :disciplinary-action
+    :class/label "Disciplinary action (expulsion, suspension, reprimand)"
+    :class/decided-by
+    "The president (学長), including a dean acting under the president's
+     delegation; the president must also define the procedure."
+    :class/patterns ["disciplin" "expulsion" "退学" "停学" "訓告" "懲戒"]
+    :class/citations
+    [(cite gakko-kyoiku-ho "学校教育法" "School Education Act"
+           "第十一条"
+           "校長及び教員は、教育上必要があると認めるときは、文部科学大臣の定めるところにより、児童、生徒及び学生に懲戒を加えることができる。ただし、体罰を加えることはできない。")
+     (cite gakko-shiko-kisoku "学校教育法施行規則" "Ordinance for Enforcement of the School Education Act"
+           "第二十六条"
+           "第2項: 懲戒のうち、退学、停学及び訓告の処分は、校長（大学にあつては、学長の委任を受けた学部長を含む。）が行う。第5項: 学長は、学生に対する退学、停学及び訓告の処分の手続を定めなければならない。")]}
+
+   {:class/id :external-authority-referral
+    :class/label
+    "Referral to, or override of, an external safety or law-enforcement authority"
+    :class/decided-by
+    "A designated human officer of the institution, not this actor. Handing
+     student personal data to a third party without the student's prior
+     consent is permitted only under an enumerated statutory exception, which
+     is a judgement about a specific case."
+    :class/patterns ["safety.*authority.*override" "law.?enforcement" "CPS"
+                     "mandatory.*report.*override" "第三者提供"]
+    :class/citations
+    [(cite appi "個人情報の保護に関する法律" "Act on the Protection of Personal Information"
+           "第二十七条"
+           "第1項: 個人情報取扱事業者は、次に掲げる場合を除くほか、あらかじめ本人の同意を得ないで、個人データを第三者に提供してはならない（一 法令に基づく場合 …）。")]}])
+
+;; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
+;; queries
+;; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+(defn class-ids
+  "Ids of every excluded decision class."
+  []
